.TH CSTR_CONSTRUCT_MP_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cstr_construct_mp_scoped \- declare and initialise a cstr with custom mprocs and RAII
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

cstr_construct_mp_scoped(s, initial, mprocs);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro combines cstr_declare_scoped() and cstr_init_mp() into one
statement. The string is destroyed automatically, through the custom memory
management procedures, when the variable leaves its scope.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        Variable name to create
initial  Initial content (C string or NULL for empty string)
mprocs   Custom memory management procedures (ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This macro needs GCC or Clang, because it uses __attribute__((cleanup))
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstr_construct_scoped (3),
.BR cstr_construct_mp (3)
